From: REG-Linux <romain.tisserand@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shadnet: fix protoc target resolution with Makefiles generator

With the CMake "Unix Makefiles" generator, add_custom_command's bare
"COMMAND protobuf::protoc" fails to resolve to the actual executable
path for the shadnet_proto_gen/shadnet.pb.cc generation step: the
literal string "protobuf::protoc" ends up in build.make instead of
the resolved binary path, and make fails with:

  make[3]: protobuf::protoc: No such file or directory
  make[3]: *** [CMakeFiles/shadps4.dir/build.make:74: shadnet_proto_gen/shadnet.pb.cc] Error 127

even though the bundled externals/protobuf protoc target builds fine.

Use the $<TARGET_FILE:...> generator expression to force explicit
path resolution, and add protobuf::protoc to DEPENDS so the target
dependency is never left implicit.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1214,12 +1214,13 @@
     OUTPUT
         "${SHADNET_PROTO_OUT}/shadnet.pb.cc"
         "${SHADNET_PROTO_OUT}/shadnet.pb.h"
-    COMMAND protobuf::protoc
+    COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:protobuf::protoc>
         "--proto_path=${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/shadnet"
         "--cpp_out=${SHADNET_PROTO_OUT}"
         "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/shadnet/shadnet.proto"
     DEPENDS
         "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/shadnet/shadnet.proto"
+        protobuf::protoc
     COMMENT "Generating shadnet protobuf sources"
     VERBATIM
 )
